1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,810
Hi.

2
00:00:00,945 --> 00:00:02,405
Let's make a planner.

3
00:00:02,485 --> 00:00:06,338
Not a mock-up, a real one: more
than thirteen hundred pages,

4
00:00:06,338 --> 00:00:09,093
where every date links to its own page.

5
00:00:09,182 --> 00:00:13,132
We'll start from a preset, look
around the editor, and export it.

6
00:00:13,245 --> 00:00:15,479
You won't need an account for any of this.

7
00:00:15,714 --> 00:00:17,744
This is PDF Architect.

8
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:19,381
The idea is simple.

9
00:00:19,485 --> 00:00:24,391
You design a handful of page layouts once,
and the app turns them into hundreds of

10
00:00:24,391 --> 00:00:27,095
pages, with the links worked out for you.

11
00:00:27,304 --> 00:00:28,974
Let's open the editor.

12
00:00:31,988 --> 00:00:35,798
The first time you open it, you
get a blank project to play with.

13
00:00:35,846 --> 00:00:40,146
I want something with content in it, so
I'll click the plus, next to the tab.

14
00:00:40,352 --> 00:00:41,992
There are three presets.

15
00:00:42,118 --> 00:00:45,108
Blank is a single, empty A4 page.

16
00:00:45,204 --> 00:00:48,804
Simple Notebook has a cover
and a few section dividers.

17
00:00:48,903 --> 00:00:53,606
And the 2026 Planner is the big
one: a year, broken into quarters,

18
00:00:53,606 --> 00:00:56,493
months and days, all linked together.

19
00:00:56,561 --> 00:00:58,131
That's the one we want.

20
00:01:03,395 --> 00:01:05,315
It takes a few seconds to build.

21
00:01:05,368 --> 00:01:09,576
And there it is: a new tab, with
every page already in place.

22
00:01:09,781 --> 00:01:11,731
The editor has three columns.

23
00:01:11,769 --> 00:01:15,512
On the left is the structure of
the document: a tree of pages,

24
00:01:15,512 --> 00:01:17,331
which the app calls nodes.

25
00:01:17,375 --> 00:01:20,575
In the middle, the canvas
shows one page at a time.

26
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:24,052
And on the right are the properties
of whatever you've selected.

27
00:01:24,564 --> 00:01:28,867
Right now the top node is selected,
so the canvas shows the year page.

28
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:33,151
The properties panel says this node
uses a template called Year View,

29
00:01:33,151 --> 00:01:36,000
and it carries one piece
of data: the year.

30
00:01:36,205 --> 00:01:41,105
Under the year sit four quarters, then
pages for weeks, notes, and to-do lists.

31
00:01:41,167 --> 00:01:43,307
The little arrow unfolds a node.

32
00:01:43,391 --> 00:01:47,246
Inside Quarter 1 are
January, February and March.

33
00:01:47,458 --> 00:01:50,612
Click January, and the
canvas switches to a month:

34
00:01:50,612 --> 00:01:55,786
a calendar where every day is a link, and
the week numbers down the side are links

35
00:01:55,786 --> 00:01:56,288
too.

36
00:01:56,495 --> 00:01:59,935
Unfold January and there's
a page for every day.

37
00:02:00,036 --> 00:02:01,956
Here's January the first.

38
00:02:01,992 --> 00:02:07,163
And each day has two pages of its own
underneath it: a journal, and daily notes.

39
00:02:07,372 --> 00:02:09,552
Now, here's the part that matters.

40
00:02:09,641 --> 00:02:13,721
Nobody sat down and drew 365 day pages.

41
00:02:13,858 --> 00:02:18,685
Switch the sidebar to Templates, and you
can see the entire planner comes from just

42
00:02:18,685 --> 00:02:19,633
ten layouts.

43
00:02:19,839 --> 00:02:21,299
I'll pick Month View.

44
00:02:21,404 --> 00:02:24,174
Up in the toolbar there's
now a Preview menu.

45
00:02:24,323 --> 00:02:28,486
It lists every node that uses this
template, and if I choose June,

46
00:02:28,486 --> 00:02:30,943
the same layout fills in with June.

47
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:32,810
That's really the whole model.

48
00:02:32,923 --> 00:02:35,243
Nodes hold the structure and the data.

49
00:02:35,318 --> 00:02:37,068
Templates hold the design.

50
00:02:37,179 --> 00:02:41,568
Change a template once, and every
page that uses it changes with it.

51
00:02:41,776 --> 00:02:43,156
Let's export it.

52
00:02:43,235 --> 00:02:48,481
The Export PDF button, up in the corner,
runs every node through its template and

53
00:02:48,481 --> 00:02:50,285
gives you a single file.

54
00:02:50,492 --> 00:02:55,546
Even at this size it only takes a few
seconds, and it all happens right here in the

55
00:02:55,546 --> 00:02:58,292
browser, so nothing is uploaded anywhere.

56
00:02:58,382 --> 00:03:02,144
The buttons next to it handle
greyscale and other devices.

57
00:03:02,256 --> 00:03:04,356
We'll get to those later in the series.

58
00:03:04,563 --> 00:03:07,503
Here's the file, open in a PDF reader.

59
00:03:07,644 --> 00:03:09,234
Page one is the year.

60
00:03:09,373 --> 00:03:11,583
These boxes aren't just labels.

61
00:03:11,732 --> 00:03:14,582
Click Quarter 2, and you land on its page.

62
00:03:14,789 --> 00:03:17,719
Each of these little
calendars is clickable too.

63
00:03:17,865 --> 00:03:19,615
Here is the second of May.

64
00:03:19,653 --> 00:03:24,437
From a day, the arrows step forward or back,
and the chips along the top jump up to

65
00:03:24,437 --> 00:03:26,763
the month, the quarter, or the year.

66
00:03:26,970 --> 00:03:29,220
None of these links were drawn by hand.

67
00:03:29,369 --> 00:03:33,661
They're worked out from the structure,
which is why they're right on every single

68
00:03:33,661 --> 00:03:34,176
page.

69
00:03:34,382 --> 00:03:36,952
So that's a complete
planner, start to finish.

70
00:03:37,025 --> 00:03:41,536
In the next episode, we'll start from
a blank page and learn the canvas:

71
00:03:41,536 --> 00:03:43,415
shapes, text, and styling.

72
00:03:43,498 --> 00:03:44,348
See you there.
